cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "mysterymaps: Geographic Mapping Tools for Healthcare Access Studies"
abstract: >-
  Builds the maps healthcare access and mystery-caller studies keep needing:
  county choropleths of provider supply, dissolved drive-time coverage surfaces
  layered as mutually exclusive alternatives, provider dot maps that stay
  clickable, and the legend, label and notes furniture those require. A single
  template assembles the common case and the pieces are exported for maps that
  are not. Also covers isochrone generation via the HERE Routing API,
  block-group overlap, Hospital Referral Region and ACOG district overlays, and
  state choropleths. Defaults encode cartographic decisions that are easy to get
  wrong: zero is its own colour class rather than the bottom of a gradient,
  legends follow the active base layer, and saved widgets stay self-contained.
type: software
